<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar buys 30,000T US corn/soy at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar buys 30,000T US corn/soy at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp said it bought a combined shipment of 25,000 tonnes of U.S. corn and 5,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans from Mitsui at a tender on Friday.  </p>
<p>The corn was bought FOB at 59.46 U.S. cents over May Chicago futures and the soybeans were purchased FOB at 68.50 U.S. cents over May Chicago futures.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p>		  Tonnage	 U.S. Gulf	 Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>    Corn	25,000	 March 6-20	 March 21-April 5</p>
<p>    Soybeans   5,000	 March 6-20	 March 21-April 5</p>
</text>
